  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\nLogic: \n\nIn each set, the three numbers are approximately **successive perfect squares** with the *square roots increasing by about +3, then +4*.\n\n√2nd=√1st+3\n\n√3rd=√2nd+4\n\n(52, 100, 196)\n\n⇒ (15 × 6) + 6 \n\n⇒ √2nd − √1st = 10 − 7.21 = **+2.79** (≈ +3)\n√3rd − √2nd = 14 − 10 = **+4**\n\n⇒ √2nd − √1st = 11.22 − 8.06 = **+3.16** (≈ +3)\n√3rd − √2nd = 15.75 − 11.22 = **+4.53** (≈ +4.5)\n\nNow, checking the options:\n\nOption 1) (72, 140, 256)\n\n⇒ √2nd − √1st = 11.83 − 8.49 = **+4.34**\n√3rd − √2nd = 16.00 − 11.83 = **+4.17**\n\nOption 2) (56, 108, 202)\n\n⇒ √2nd − √1st = 10.39 − 7.48 = **+2.91**\n√3rd − √2nd = 14.21 − 10.39 = **+3.82**\n\nOption 3) **(68, 132, 260)**\n\n**⇒ √2nd − √1st = 11.83 − 8.49 =** **+3.34**\n**√3rd − √2nd = 16.00 − 11.83 =** **+4.17**\n\nMatches the pattern (+3, +4)\n\nOption 4) (94, 184, 264)\n\n⇒ √2nd − √1st = 13.56 − 9.70 = **+3.86**\n√3rd − √2nd = 16.25 − 13.56 = **+2.69**\n\nHence, the correct option is \"Option 3\"",
